# Development defaults. Confirm capacity and retention before production.
DATABASE_PATH=/var/lib/workbench/workbench.db
ATTACHMENT_PATH=/var/lib/workbench/attachments
ATTACHMENT_MAX_BYTES=5242880
ATTACHMENT_MAX_PIXELS=20000000
ATTACHMENT_MAX_PER_OBJECT=10
ATTACHMENT_MAX_TOTAL_BYTES=5368709120
ATTACHMENT_MAX_CONCURRENT=2
# After npm run build, with these environment variables securely loaded:
# umask 077
# npm run backup -- --output /approved/local/staging/unique-empty-directory
# npm run restore:verify -- --manifest /approved/local/staging/backup/manifest.json --scratch /isolated/empty-restore
# Verification never opens the live database. For an operational drill, start the
# application against the isolated restored database AND its attachments directory.
# Staging must be outside the public web root and owned by the service/backup user.
# No registered attachment deletion/GC is supported: snapshot copies rely on immutability.
# A crash before DB registration can leave an unreferenced file; do not delete it
# while an upload or backup is running. There is no automatic cleanup/retention job.
#
# A directory on the same machine is NOT an off-instance backup.
# Before production: configure user-managed authenticated encryption (e.g. age
# recipient public key; private key held separately), encrypt the complete backup,
# and transfer it to an explicitly approved independent host/bucket via verified
# SSH/SFTP or authenticated TLS. Verify remote encrypted archive hash/receipt, then
# decrypt in an isolated machine and run restore:verify + login/business replay.
# Never put credentials, private keys or passphrases in this file, command arguments
# or logs. These tools neither perform remote transfer nor claim encrypted backup.
# Alert on nonzero exit / missing completed manifest, disk/quota errors and overdue
# independently verified transfers. Keep failed partial staging private for diagnosis.
# Proposed schedule: daily; retain 7 daily + 4 weekly copies (user-confirmed policy).
# Proposed RPO <=24h / RTO <=4h require measured off-instance drills, not local claims.
# Full drill before first deployment; monthly sample restore thereafter.
# Example operator-run encryption/transfer recipe AFTER destination approval:
# Set BACKUP_DIR, RECIPIENTS_FILE (public recipient keys), ENCRYPTED_ARCHIVE,
# and APPROVED_DESTINATION in the operator's private shell configuration.
# set -euo pipefail
# tar -C "$BACKUP_DIR" -cf - . | age -R "$RECIPIENTS_FILE" -o "$ENCRYPTED_ARCHIVE"
# scp -o StrictHostKeyChecking=yes "$ENCRYPTED_ARCHIVE" "$APPROVED_DESTINATION"
# Pin/verify the host key beforehand through a trusted channel; use SSH agent or
# another user-managed credential provider. Verify remote hash/receipt separately.
# Do not mark the backup successful off-host until independent decrypt+restore pass.
# Manifest hashes detect corruption/inventory mismatch; they are not signatures.
# Authenticate the encrypted archive/manifest against malicious wholesale replacement.
